  "id": "conditioned-suppression",
  "term": "conditioned suppression",
  "definition": "Conditioned suppression is a learned reduction in reward-seeking behavior when the situation has become associated with adverse conditions. In this packet, it refers specifically to decreased seeking of palatable food in an aversive context.",
